  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2025-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Modulo \\(22,\\) the equation gives \\(13x \\equiv 4,\\) so \\(x \\equiv 2 \\pmod{22}.\\) With \\(57x \\lt 400,\\) the only option is \\(x = 2,\\) which gives \\(22y = 286,\\) so \\(y = 13.\\) Then \\(x + y = 15.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Reduce \\(57x + 22y = 400\\) modulo \\(22\\) to pin down \\(x\\)",
        "Since \\(x\\) is positive and \\(57x \\lt 400,\\) only a few values of \\(x\\) are possible"
      ],
